WEBVTT

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:23.890
<i>Every day I keep wondering if</i>
<i>there's something missing.</i>

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:31.230
<i>I still want to keep feeling my</i>
<i>heart beating in anticipation.</i>

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:38.970
<i>Ideals are far out of reach, but</i>
<i>reality is within my grasp.</i>

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:45.040
<i>It's not easy standing against the wind,</i>
<i>but as long as I keep smiling...</i>

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:49.820
<i>... staying true to myself,</i>
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:57.590
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll find him and take my chance.</i>

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:04.560
<i>I'll make the whole world stop</i>
<i>to see the angel that I'll be.</i>

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:12.500
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll meet the man of my dreams.</i>

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:20.170
<i>Nothing can slow me down. Tomorrow</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i>

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:31.260
Okay. That'll be ¥290.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:32.860
Thanks.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.530
Don't you want a bag?

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:37.500
No thanks. Trying to save our resources.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:40.030
"Pasteurized Milk"

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:50.240
Nothing beats this enriched low-
temp-pasteurized milk!

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:54.470
"Recycling Bin"

00:01:55.250 --> 00:02:00.210
That's awful! You'll never grow big and
strong if you keep eating such junk!

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:07.690
I'm going to be 154 cm tall and
weigh 45 kg! No matter what!

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:10.230
Then I can become
a policewoman!

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.460
What a weirdo.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:22.970
FILE. 31
THE 40-BELOW
DUEL

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:26.010
"Police Station"

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:29.480
Hmm... What a
gorgeous day!

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:31.040
You said it.

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:36.680
Makes me wish we were going for
a joy ride rather than on patrol.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:41.650
Detective Tokuno! Good morning!
Beautiful day, isn't it?

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.790
Ah, he practically
ignored me!

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:49.940
I'm sure he's got a lot on his
mind with that new case.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:55.800
He must be busy with the investigation
since they haven't arrested anyone.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.540
Huh? What case?

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:00.100
Natsumi, don't you remember?

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.650
No clue.

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:02.740
Unbelievable.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:08.350
<i>"The OX Pharmaceutical Bio-Research</i>
<i>Center was robbed this morning."</i>
"OX Biological Research Center"

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:11.220
<i>"3 similar cases have been reported in</i>
<i>the Tokyo area in the last 2 months."</i>

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:11.290
<i>"Hey, look! There's Detective Tokuno!"</i>

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.230
"Police have determined that the same
<i>person or group is responsible..."</i>

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:16.250
<i>"Natsumi, I can't see!"</i>
<i>"...and are continuing their investigation."</i>

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:20.760
Oh! What?!
That case?!

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:23.770
I only paid attention to Det. Tokuno.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.570
Why doesn't that surprise me?

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:26.660
Hey! Wait for me!

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:34.470
Have you lost your
way, ma'am?

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:40.450
Yes, I'm looking for
the bus stop.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:44.920
Up there, turn right at the fourth
street and go up the hill...

00:03:56.570 --> 00:04:01.770
She's doing her stuff, our
little junior policewoman.

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:04.430
My mentors! Natsumi!
Miyuki!

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:08.180
I keep telling you to
quit calling us that!

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:18.980
You ignored the light!

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:21.230
You get a fine!
You get a fine!

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:24.500
People who don't obey the
traffic laws get arrested!

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:26.630
You'll get arrested!

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:28.560
Hey, you guys...

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:30.070
Aren't you?

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.230
Who are you?

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:34.970
I know this
big girl.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:39.310
She's friends with Natsumi
and Miyuki.

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:42.180
Really? Well, what makes
you so special?

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:44.650
Yeah, what gives?

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:48.280
That's silly. You listen
to me, children.

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:51.080
My name is Saori Saga.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:57.290
I'm not just friends with Natsumi and
Miyuki. They're my mentors.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:58.730
Understand?

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.160
Men-tors? Men-tors?

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:03.330
That's right.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:08.170
You see... I'm like a special
assistant to them...

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:12.010
...ready to be of service when-
ever they need me.

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:14.270
That's how it is.

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:20.580
We're in charge of making sure every-
one obeys the traffic rules.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:25.180
That means you have to do everything
we tell you to do.

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.050
I work for Miyuki!

00:05:27.230 --> 00:05:28.350
I work for Natsumi!

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:30.260
And I...

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.990
Don't you work
for Ken?

00:05:33.170 --> 00:05:35.000
Yeah, Ken!

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:38.230
I want a girl!

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:39.740
All right,
all right.

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:41.810
Okay, you have to
come with us.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:43.630
Yeah, come
with us.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:45.680
Come with
us.

00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:47.070
Come on,
let's go!

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:48.170
Let's go!

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:49.150
<i>Well, it is important for officers to get</i>
<i>to know people in the community.</i>

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:54.880
Come on, let's go! Hurry up, let's go!

00:05:55.460 --> 00:06:00.620
Okay you guys, I'll show you
how to be a policewoman.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:03.430
Hey! Wait
for us!

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:27.750
All right. When you find something
someone has left behind...

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:30.620
...you should take
it to the police.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:31.520
I know that.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:33.280
Everybody knows you've
got to do that.

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:34.530
Yeah!

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:42.320
That's the most important thing about the
lost-and-found game. Ready to play?

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:45.100
"The lost-and-found
game?"

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:48.670
Right. In this game, the winner
is the first person...

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:53.010
...to find something lost and turn
it over to Natsumi or Miyuki.

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:55.300
I've never heard of
that game before.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:57.510
We don't have that game
at the school olympics.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:59.280
No, we don't.

00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:03.080
Exactly! They don't teach you
this game in preschool.

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:07.420
This is a difficult training exercise that
helps you become a police officer.

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:08.460
Really?

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:09.990
I think you're
lying.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:12.760
Yeah, you're not
telling the truth.

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:15.530
Come on, we're going
to start. Ready? Go!

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:21.270
That big girl sure
likes to run a lot.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:24.270
I think she's trying
to trick us.

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:26.540
We won't let her!

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:29.200
Yeah, we'll finish
first!

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:30.680
Yeah!

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:33.220
Hey! Wait
for me!

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:01.270
Someone left this behind
and I found it!

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:22.600
Damn!

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:27.570
"Fire Hydrant"

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:28.900
Hey, that reminds me.

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:30.870
Yeah?

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:33.740
Tokuno's working on a burglary at
a bioresearch company, right?

00:08:33.850 --> 00:08:38.010
But what would anybody want
to steal from there?

00:08:38.420 --> 00:08:42.180
Something to do with ex-
perimental bacteria.

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:48.450
Bac... Bacteria? Bacteria,
you mean, as in germs?!

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:50.990
Yeah. Why do
you ask?

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:58.130
'Cause! Maybe it's a case where germs
get out and everybody gets it and dies.

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:00.370
You know, like with the Zubola virus.

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:02.270
E-bo-la virus.

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:07.010
I don't think it's anything
that serious. Hey!

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:09.520
My mentors!

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.210
"Downpour Brand Pasteurized Milk"

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.920
We're sure running into her a lot today.

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:15.150
Yeah.

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:18.450
Here. Somebody
lost this.

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:21.790
You... brought
this for us?

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:25.430
Yes. At approximately
3;15 this afternoon...

00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:29.090
...it was left behind in a phone booth
in front of the "Deen" restaurant.

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:32.030
Well. Thanks a lot for
bringing it to us.

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:33.870
By the way...

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:38.910
Did Yuuta, Shou, and Maho
come and see you?

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:40.980
No, not at all.
How come?

00:09:41.150 --> 00:09:42.640
Great!

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:46.950
See you later! Have
a good day!

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:52.450
Have a good
day.

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:54.490
I will.

00:10:01.670 --> 00:10:05.100
And that's that. Now all I have
to do is find the kids.

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:06.570
I've found you.

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:24.290
You're the one who took a black brief-
case out of the telephone booth...

00:10:24.460 --> 00:10:25.920
...weren't you?

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:29.530
Oh, was that
yours?

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:33.570
Gee, if you saw me take it you could
have at least said something.

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:38.360
Forget that, and tell
me where it is.

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:42.700
Don't worry, I turned
it in to the police.

00:11:07.030 --> 00:11:09.060
I can't find any
lost stuff.

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:11.030
Me either.

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:13.130
Hey!

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:14.300
Look!

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:16.380
We found something!

00:11:20.010 --> 00:11:22.140
That's Saori in
the picture.

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:26.270
That's dumb. She went and
lost something herself!

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:27.380
Let's go!

00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:28.540
Okay.
Okay.

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:31.690
Hup-two! Hup-two!
Hup-two!

00:11:43.070 --> 00:11:44.730
We're back!
We're back!

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:46.270
Hello.

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:47.340
Hey.

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:49.410
What's that?

00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:51.940
Somebody lost this.

00:11:52.110 --> 00:11:53.910
All right.

00:11:54.010 --> 00:11:56.480
We'd better find out what's
in this thing.

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:59.780
What do you mean? It's
not a present for us?

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:02.920
You don't actually think we'd
bring you octopus balls...

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:06.120
...or sweet rice cakes in
a briefcase, do you?

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:07.880
It's got an electronic lock.

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:10.820
I wish it was
food!

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:13.730
Or technical plans for a
new vacuum cleaner.

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:15.930
I say a gun and
cutlet on rice.

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:17.900
I say counterfeit cash and
salmon eggs on rice.

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:20.040
I say a time bomb and
Chinese food.

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:22.070
What?! A bomb?!

00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:22.680
Look out, Kobayakawa! I'll save you!

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:23.880
Stop!

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:24.010
Look out, Kobayakawa! I'll save you!

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:24.140
It's not what you think!

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:26.080
Let me through! Hurry!

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:31.040
Hey! Isn't someone going
to answer the phone?

00:12:33.550 --> 00:12:35.380
Hello. Traffic Section.

00:12:36.260 --> 00:12:38.520
I can't open it.

00:12:39.460 --> 00:12:43.050
It's some kind of
special lock.

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:45.630
So special that even
you can't open it?

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:47.730
What is this
thing?

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:51.430
Hey! Tsujimoto! Kobayakawa!
It's for you!

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:53.400
Thank you.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:55.840
Hello?

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:59.640
Oh, hi Saori. Thanks for
turning in that... Huh?

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:01.740
What's the
matter?

00:13:01.850 --> 00:13:03.510
The case you
brought us?

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:05.510
You found
him?

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:09.610
Hey, your break's over.
Get back to work.

00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:13.220
Yeah? And who's?

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:18.390
The case belongs to a
friend of my father.

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:20.800
Yes. A real coincidence.

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:27.260
Yes. Anyway, he needs it back, other-
wise he'll be in big trouble at work.

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:32.640
Right. He wants you to bring it over
without involving anyone else.

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:36.700
Yes. Make sure you two police-
women come alone.

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:43.520
All right. We'll be at the entrance to the
Tsukiji warehouses in 30 minutes.

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:49.260
She found the
owner?

00:13:49.630 --> 00:13:51.430
Yes.

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:53.170
What is it?

00:13:53.170 --> 00:13:54.500
What is it?
"Policewomen?"

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:54.570
"Policewomen?"

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:55.560
Huh?
"Policewomen?"

00:13:55.740 --> 00:14:01.300
Saori called us "policewomen." Doesn't
that strike you as odd? It's unlike her.

00:14:01.470 --> 00:14:02.570
Fill me in.

00:14:05.750 --> 00:14:08.810
So Saori's started acting
strange all of a sudden.

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:12.720
And it's hard to believe she found the
owner of that case by coincidence.

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:16.250
And the case has a
special lock on it.

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:25.850
Sounds like an interesting case.
Sure you don't need backup?

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:29.160
Well, we don't know for sure whether
there's even been a crime.

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:39.480
Hi.

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:41.700
Detective Tokuno.

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:45.540
Wonder what they're
up to today...

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:51.210
Hup-two! Hup-two!
Hup-two!

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:52.250
Hi!

00:14:52.430 --> 00:14:53.290
Natsumi!

00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:54.150
Miyuki!

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:54.850
Look!

00:14:55.030 --> 00:14:56.300
Sorry, we're in a bit of a rush.

00:14:56.300 --> 00:14:57.850
And we can't stop on the road...

00:14:57.960 --> 00:14:59.630
We found this, so you should take it.

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:02.300
We found it!

00:15:02.470 --> 00:15:05.100
Sorry you guys, but
we're really...

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:07.130
Take a look at this, Miyuki.

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:10.940
Saori lost this.

00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:11.840
We had a race to find lost stuff!

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:12.950
I'm sure it's hers.

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:13.140
She lost her own bag!

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:14.340
Thanks, kids.

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:16.910
That's dumb!

00:15:34.900 --> 00:15:36.870
Saori?! Are you here?

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:45.400
Saori?!

00:15:45.580 --> 00:15:46.410
My mentors!

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:52.570
So you're the friend of her father's,
who lost the case.

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:56.890
Yeah. That's the part
I'm playing anyway.

00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:00.980
Hurry up and hand
over the case!

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:06.590
What are you doing?!
Hurry up and get it!

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:10.500
I didn't even see
them there.

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:12.140
Me either.

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:16.930
Hey, old man. How about
cooling off a bit?

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:20.610
It's your fault for not delivering
it properly in the first place!

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:29.020
I knew that I shouldn't have
dealt with you directly.

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:34.960
What are you doing? Hurry up
and give me that bacteria!

00:16:36.460 --> 00:16:43.800
B... Bacteria? You mean it was the Zubola
virus that was stolen from the lab?

00:16:45.970 --> 00:16:48.300
Oh, my heart will
dissolve!

00:16:50.180 --> 00:16:53.540
This is a unique strain of lactobacillus!
It has to be treated with care!

00:16:53.910 --> 00:16:56.440
Huh?! Lactobacillus?
Huh?! Lactobacillus?

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:58.610
What's lactobacillus?

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:00.250
You fool!

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:05.160
How could you not even know that?!
It's the bacteria that breaks down...

00:17:05.260 --> 00:17:10.750
...sugars in the body during lactic
fermentation in dairy products.

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:14.390
It promotes growth
in intes...

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:25.910
Growth!

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:29.410
I... I want some
of that!

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:31.550
What's this?!

00:17:31.720 --> 00:17:33.910
Got it!

00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:37.150
You wench!

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:39.120
Aah! I can't
see!

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:42.120
This'll stop you!

00:17:59.950 --> 00:18:03.180
Oh no, you don't!

00:18:05.920 --> 00:18:06.520
Natsumi!

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:06.920
Okay!

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:11.320
Stop right
there!

00:18:15.930 --> 00:18:17.050
Over there!

00:18:35.150 --> 00:18:36.940
I'm freezing!

00:18:37.120 --> 00:18:40.980
What'd you tell us to come in here
for? Didn't you have a plan?

00:18:41.150 --> 00:18:43.880
Sorry. I wasn't
thinking.

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:45.320
We'll freeze
to death!

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:54.270
So, you want to die by freezing, so
you can stay beautiful forever?

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:55.930
I'll pass.

00:18:56.100 --> 00:18:58.760
You've got to be kidding!
I'll never forgive you!

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:02.460
Even if I live to be a
dried up old hag!

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:06.340
All right, let's have
the briefcase.

00:19:06.510 --> 00:19:08.480
Yes, let's.

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:14.310
As I recall, police like to first
fire a few shots as a bluff.

00:19:15.350 --> 00:19:19.020
Huh? What the?

00:19:19.460 --> 00:19:22.990
That's right! His gun won't
fire in this cold!

00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:30.240
The tables have turned,
gentlemen!

00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:33.570
Unlike your gun, this super air
gun isn't affected by the cold!

00:19:33.670 --> 00:19:37.670
The bullets weigh 0.3 grams,
and travel up to 90 km/hour.

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:39.870
You can bet they're
painful.

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:49.780
The air hose exploded!
It's frozen!

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:51.790
Your luck's run
out, gals!

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:55.450
When all else fails! Saori!
Hang onto this!

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:57.830
Okay!

00:19:58.230 --> 00:19:59.860
Take this!

00:20:01.030 --> 00:20:02.900
And that! And this!
And that!

00:20:04.540 --> 00:20:06.830
And this! And that!
And this!

00:20:26.060 --> 00:20:27.030
Detective Tokuno!

00:20:27.730 --> 00:20:30.090
Hey Tsujimoto, Kobayakawa!

00:20:30.930 --> 00:20:36.800
Thanks to you, we were able to arrest
these bacteria thieves. Thank you.

00:20:38.770 --> 00:20:39.830
Yes, sir.
Yes, sir.

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:43.170
That means you, too,
junior policewoman.

00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:48.180
Thank you very
much, sir.

00:20:53.650 --> 00:20:55.980
"Special Formula Milk"

00:20:58.660 --> 00:21:01.490
Saori, let's play the lost-and-found game!

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:02.890
Yeah, come on!

00:21:03.060 --> 00:21:06.730
I can't today. Anyway, good kids
go straight home. Go on, now.

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:10.360
How come?
Saori! Come on, play with us!

00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:13.300
Hi! How are
you kids?

00:21:13.470 --> 00:21:17.070
There's Natsumi and Miyuki!
Wanna play with us?

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:18.480
Huh? He didn't mean it
was good for growth...

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:20.950
"Growth"

00:21:20.950 --> 00:21:21.040
Huh? He didn't mean it
was good for growth...

00:21:21.180 --> 00:21:26.050
...he meant it was good for
"lntestinal Regularity"

00:21:27.190 --> 00:21:33.590
So even if I drink this new kind
of milk, I still won't grow big?

00:21:34.090 --> 00:21:39.290
Yeah, instead of worrying about your
height, brush up on your studies.

00:21:39.470 --> 00:21:41.490
You're one to
talk, Natsumi.

00:21:41.670 --> 00:21:42.970
Let's play! Come on!

00:21:42.970 --> 00:21:45.330
Let's play! Come on!
Sorry, kids. We're on duty.

00:21:47.270 --> 00:21:50.240
I won't grow big?

00:21:55.310 --> 00:22:00.820
<i>Every time I fall</i>
<i>out of love...</i>

00:22:03.820 --> 00:22:11.430
<i>... everything that I see</i>
<i>turns monochrome.</i>

00:22:12.030 --> 00:22:18.330
<i>We often used to go see the</i>
<i>games at the stadium...</i>

00:22:18.440 --> 00:22:28.450
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:28.510 --> 00:22:42.390
<i>Even after you've gone, I still wanna</i>
<i>tell the world what it is that I love.</i>

00:22:42.690 --> 00:22:50.640
<i>Looking up to the sky, I try</i>
<i>holding back the tears.</i>

00:22:50.700 --> 00:22:59.280
<i>Flags were moving in the wind and</i>
<i>things seemed brighter yesterday.</i>

00:22:59.510 --> 00:23:07.310
<i>Looking up to the sky, we used</i>
<i>to talk about our dreams.</i>

00:23:07.420 --> 00:23:16.890
<i>No matter how far out of reach they seemed,</i>
<i>dreams could come true, or so it felt.</i>

00:23:17.300 --> 00:23:24.370
<i>Tell me that that fire in your</i>
<i>eyes was not a lie.</i>

00:23:28.310 --> 00:23:32.440
Shouldn't riders shift their weight while
cornering in a car, like on a bike?

00:23:32.610 --> 00:23:36.210
Nope. By the way, that's
'driver,' not 'rider.'

00:23:36.380 --> 00:23:43.650
But, while cornering, you hafta... y'know,
sidecars... wait, those are 3-wheelers...

00:23:43.820 --> 00:23:46.590
Next time, You're Under Arrest, File 32...

00:23:46.660 --> 00:23:47.890
..."Blast off! Natsumi's Supermachine!"

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:50.530
Y'know, you gotta shift,
er... like THlllSS...
